`buildStickerGallery` trims the query. If the trimmed query has fewer than two Unicode code units, return `invalid` even when an error is supplied. Otherwise, a non-null error returns `error`. Malformed records—non-integer IDs, empty image strings, or non-array/non-string tags—must be ignored. Valid records match when any tag contains the trimmed query case-insensitively. Preserve record order and tag order. Return `empty` when no valid records match. Returned item and tag objects must be copies, and inputs must not be mutated.

